{
    "background_story": "Santana grew up in a small town where music was a way of life. As a child, she would often watch her grandfather, a blues musician, play his guitar on the porch. One day, he handed her a nickel-plated harmonica and taught her how to play. Santana's love for music was born, and she spent hours practicing on that harmonica. As she grew older, she began to perform on street corners, earning nickels and dimes from passersby. Her talent eventually caught the attention of a local music producer, who offered her a record deal. Santana's soulful voice and harmonica playing made her a star, but she never forgot her humble beginnings. She continued to play on street corners, now as a way to give back to her community and inspire others to chase their dreams, just as that nickel-plated harmonica had inspired her.",
